content.text:
Now CSS. Append R12 styles. Need to consider `.format-block` layout on mobile and existing `.mode-switch` margin. Add:

```
/* R12 — Formato de ronda: 1 palabra o 5 palabras */
.format-block{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;margin:0 0 10px;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #ffffff10;border-radius:9px;background:#1c1d22}
.format-heading{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#a6a6ad}
.format-switch{width:auto}
.format-switch button{padding:5px 9px;font-size:8px}
.prompt-words{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:6px;margin-top:14px}
.prompt-words[hidden]{display:none}
.prompt-word-chip{min-height:52px;display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;padding:8px 4px;border:1px solid #d2f36b38;border-radius:8px;background:#2a2d22;color:var(--lime);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(12px,1.3vw,17px);letter-spacing:.4px;line-height:1.1;opacity:0;transform:translateY(4px);transition:opacity .2s,transform .2s}
.prompt-word-chip.visible{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}
body.mode-double .prompt-word-chip{border-color:#fb718538;background:#2c2024;color:#fb7185}
@media(max-width:590px){
  .format-block{padding:7px 10px}
  .format-heading{font-size:8px}
  .format-switch button{padding:4px 7px;font-size:7px}
  .prompt-words{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:5px}
  .prompt-word-chip{min-height:42px;font-size:13px}
  .prompt-words .prompt-word-chip:last-child:nth-child(odd){grid-column:1/-1}
}
```

Wait `body.mode-double .prompt-word-chip` color: in doble mode, the lime variable is pink, so `color:var(--lime)` already pink. The background and border could use `#fb7185` but not necessary. Remove or keep subtle.

Also `.format-block` might increase card height; okay. At mobile, format block row: heading + buttons, fits 343? heading ~100 + buttons ~140 + gap = 250, fits.

Need `.prompt-word[hidden]{display:none}`? UA hidden works, but `.prompt-word` has `transition` and `margin-top`; hidden attribute sets display:none in UA stylesheet; our CSS doesn't set display, so fine. Add explicit for safety:
```
.prompt-word[hidden]{display:none}
```
But `.prompt-word` might be `display:block` default; hidden works.

Also `.prompt-words` chips need animation; `requestAnimationFrame` adds visible. If user has reduced motion, transition-duration is .01ms, fine.

Let's append CSS.

