content.text:
Now add functions setCharacter/toggleCharacter/drawCharacter/updateCharacterUI near setTermination, and resetSession clear.

Implementation:

```js
function setCharacter(enabled) {
  state.characterOn = Boolean(enabled);
  if (!state.characterOn) {
    state.currentCharacter = null;
  } else if (!state.currentCharacter) {
    state.currentCharacter = drawCharacter();
  }
  updateCharacterUI();
  saveProgress();
}

function toggleCharacter() {
  state.characterOn = !state.characterOn;
  if (state.characterOn) {
    state.currentCharacter = drawCharacter();
  } else {
    state.currentCharacter = null;
  }
  updateCharacterUI();
  saveProgress();
  showToast(state.characterOn
    ? `Personaje activado: ${state.currentCharacter?.name || 'en la próxima ronda'}.`
    : 'Personaje desactivado.');
}

function drawCharacter() {
  if (!state.characterDeck.length) {
    const fresh = CHARACTERS.filter((item) => item !== state.currentCharacter);
    state.characterDeck = shuffle(fresh.length ? fresh : CHARACTERS);
  }
  return state.characterDeck.shift() || CHARACTERS[0];
}

function updateCharacterUI() {
  const on = state.characterOn;
  ui.characterToggle.classList.toggle('active', on);
  ui.characterToggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on));
  ui.characterState.textContent = on ? 'ON' : 'OFF';
  const visible = on && Boolean(state.currentCharacter);
  ui.characterChip.hidden = !visible;
  if (visible) {
    ui.characterName.textContent = state.currentCharacter.name;
    ui.characterRule.textContent = state.currentCharacter.rule;
  }
}
```

Place after updateTerminationUI. On reset: `state.characterDeck = []; state.currentCharacter = null;` and call `updateCharacterUI()` after `updateTerminationUI()`.

Note: `setCharacter` at init: `state.characterOn` from saved, if true and no currentCharacter, draw one immediately. This means on page load with character ON, the chip shows a character even before starting. Is that okay? The acceptance says the character appears with the word; before starting, there's no word. Maybe we shouldn't show it until a round starts. The chip would show above "LISTA" while idle, which is odd. Better: `setCharacter` at init should not draw a character if idle; only set the toggle state. When a round starts, draw. But when toggled ON mid-round, draw immediately. And if toggled ON while idle, maybe don't draw until the first round.

Distinguish init vs user toggle: `setCharacter(enabled, draw = false)`. At init call `setCharacter(state.characterOn)` without drawing. `toggleCharacter` calls `setCharacter(!state.characterOn, true)`.

Simpler:

```js
function setCharacter(enabled, drawNow = false) {
  state.characterOn = Boolean(enabled);
  if (!state.characterOn) state.currentCharacter = null;
  else if (drawNow) state.currentCharacter = drawCharacter();
  updateCharacterUI();
  saveProgress();
}

function toggleCharacter() {
  const next = !state.characterOn;
  setCharacter(next, next);
  showToast(next ? ... : ...);
}
```

If toggled ON mid-round, draw. If toggled ON idle, draw now too; the chip shows a character with "LISTA". Is that bad? Maybe it's actually a nice preview. But "aparece junto a la palabra" — with LISTA it's fine as a preview. However, on page load with saved ON, `setCharacter(state.characterOn)` with drawNow false → no chip until first round. But if the user toggles ON while idle, it shows a character immediately, then the first round draws another character. Slight inconsistency but acceptable. To keep it consistent, when toggled ON while idle, don't draw; the first round will draw. When toggled ON while running, draw immediately for the current round.

```js
function toggleCharacter() {
  const next = !state.characterOn;
  setCharacter(next, next && state.running);
  ...
}
```

Then if toggled ON while idle, chip hidden until the first round; toast says "Personaje activado. Aparece al empezar la ronda." If toggled ON while running, chip appears now. Good.

But if toggled ON while running and `state.currentCharacter` is null, draw. If toggled OFF then ON while running, draw a new one. Fine.

`setCharacter(next, true)` draws even if currentCharacter exists (e.g., toggling ON after OFF). Fine.

At init, `setCharacter(state.characterOn)` with drawNow false. Good.

When a new round starts, `drawCharacter` sets currentCharacter. Good.

`updateCharacterUI` visible only if on && currentCharacter. Good.

Reset: currentCharacter null, updateCharacterUI hides chip.

Toast wording:
- ON while running: `Personaje activado: EL VECINO.`
- ON while idle: `Personaje activado. Aparece al empezar la ronda.`
- OFF: `Personaje desactivado.`

Let's add.

